A large automobile manufacturer plans to optimize its supply chain network. The company has two factories (F1 and F2), one parts supplier (S), and one distribution center (DC). The daily production capacities of factories F1 and F2 are 500 and 400 cars, respectively, while the daily processing capacity of the distribution center is 600 cars. The parts supplier can provide 1000 sets of parts per day.

The transportation cost from the supplier to the factories is 1 yuan per set of parts, and the transportation cost from the factories to the distribution center is 2 yuan per car. The production cost of factory F1 is 10 yuan per car, and the production cost of factory F2 is 8 yuan per car.

Your task is to develop a supply chain network design that meets the following objectives:
- Minimize total cost;
- Ensure the stability and continuous operation of the supply chain;
- Maximize the utilization of the factories and the distribution center.

In addition, the following constraints need to be considered:
- Capacity constraints: The production capacities of the factories and the distribution center cannot exceed their maximum capacities;
- Parts supply constraint: The parts demand of the factories cannot exceed the supply of the supplier.

How should the optimal supply chain network design be formulated while satisfying all the above objectives and constraints?

